{
  "CompatRange": {
    "description": "spec \u00a73.5 `compat: {asset_classes, timeframes, min_history}`.",
    "properties": {
      "asset_classes": {
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "minItems": 1,
        "title": "Asset Classes",
        "type": "array"
      },
      "min_history_days": {
        "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
        "title": "Min History Days",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "schema_version": {
        "const": "v1",
        "default": "v1",
        "title": "Schema Version",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "timeframes": {
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "minItems": 1,
        "title": "Timeframes",
        "type": "array"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "asset_classes",
      "timeframes",
      "min_history_days"
    ],
    "title": "CompatRange",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "ListingPrice": {
    "$defs": {
      "PriceKind": {
        "description": "spec \u00a73.5 `price: OneTime|Subscription{period, trial_days}`.",
        "enum": [
          "ONE_TIME",
          "SUBSCRIPTION"
        ],
        "title": "PriceKind",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "SubscriptionTerms": {
        "description": "spec \u00a73.5 `price: Subscription{period, trial_days}`.\n\n`period_days` spells out the billing period as a concrete integer\n(rather than a free-text cadence like \"monthly\") because MP-6\n(`domain/subscription_rules.py`, period-key/pro-rated-refund math)\nneeds a number to compute `(subscription_id, period_start)` idempotency\nkeys (\u00a75) -- deferring that shape choice to MP-6 would mean re-touching\nthis contract then.",
        "properties": {
          "period_days": {
            "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
            "title": "Period Days",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "schema_version": {
            "const": "v1",
            "default": "v1",
            "title": "Schema Version",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "trial_days": {
            "default": 0,
            "minimum": 0,
            "title": "Trial Days",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "period_days"
        ],
        "title": "SubscriptionTerms",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    "description": "spec \u00a73.5 `price: OneTime|Subscription{...}` union, modeled as a\ntagged `kind` instead of a Python union type so `model_json_schema()`\nproduces a stable, diffable shape for the snapshot test (a `Union`\nrenders as `anyOf` and reorders across pydantic point releases --\ntests/foundation/unit/ai/gateway saw this exact class of instability,\nsee requirements-lock.txt's pydantic pin note).",
    "properties": {
      "amount": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
            "type": "number"
          },
          {
            "pattern": "^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Amount"
      },
      "currency": {
        "maxLength": 3,
        "minLength": 3,
        "title": "Currency",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "kind": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/PriceKind"
      },
      "schema_version": {
        "const": "v1",
        "default": "v1",
        "title": "Schema Version",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "subscription": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SubscriptionTerms"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ],
        "default": null
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "kind",
      "amount",
      "currency"
    ],
    "title": "ListingPrice",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "ReproductionKey": {
    "description": "spec \u00a73.4 `reproducibility_key = sha256(script_hash ||\ndata_lineage_hash || rollup_version || config_hash || model_hash)`.\n\nEvery input component is carried alongside the final digest (`key`) --\nnot just the opaque hex string -- so a listing can be re-verified\nagainst a later backtest run (MP-11's `verify_listing_backtest.py`)\nwithout needing to re-derive lineage out of a single hash. Composing\n`key` from the other fields is BT-1's job (`src/foundation/backtest`);\nthis contract only validates that all five components and the digest\nare well-formed hex strings.",
    "properties": {
      "config_hash": {
        "maxLength": 64,
        "minLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "title": "Config Hash",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "data_lineage_hash": {
        "maxLength": 64,
        "minLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "title": "Data Lineage Hash",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "key": {
        "maxLength": 64,
        "minLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "title": "Key",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "model_hash": {
        "maxLength": 64,
        "minLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "title": "Model Hash",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "rollup_version": {
        "minLength": 1,
        "title": "Rollup Version",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "schema_version": {
        "const": "v1",
        "default": "v1",
        "title": "Schema Version",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "script_hash": {
        "maxLength": 64,
        "minLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "title": "Script Hash",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "script_hash",
      "data_lineage_hash",
      "rollup_version",
      "config_hash",
      "model_hash",
      "key"
    ],
    "title": "ReproductionKey",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "ReputationSnapshot": {
    "description": "spec \u00a73.5 `ReputationScore{verified_runs, reproduced_backtests,\ndispute_rate, weighted_score}`; \u00a74.3 gives the weighting formula\n(`0.5*f(verified_runs) + 0.3*g(reproduced_backtests) +\n0.2*(1 - dispute_rate)`) that MP-4's `domain/reputation.py` computes --\n`weighted_score` here is a *reported* value this contract accepts as\ngiven, not a value it derives, which is what keeps MP-1 schema-only.",
    "properties": {
      "dispute_rate": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "maximum": 1.0,
            "minimum": 0.0,
            "type": "number"
          },
          {
            "pattern": "^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Dispute Rate"
      },
      "reproduced_backtests": {
        "minimum": 0,
        "title": "Reproduced Backtests",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "schema_version": {
        "const": "v1",
        "default": "v1",
        "title": "Schema Version",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "verified_runs": {
        "minimum": 0,
        "title": "Verified Runs",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "weighted_score": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "maximum": 1.0,
            "minimum": 0.0,
            "type": "number"
          },
          {
            "pattern": "^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Weighted Score"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "verified_runs",
      "reproduced_backtests",
      "dispute_rate",
      "weighted_score"
    ],
    "title": "ReputationSnapshot",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "ScriptListing": {
